 # Add Tattler receive cooperative interruption tool
 
-
+Design a Tattler-level cooperative interruption tool. When busy and pending inbox gets its first message, send at most one nudge telling the model pending Tattler messages exist and it may call tattler_receive if they may affect current work. The tattler_receive tool should be sequential/called alone, have a call renderer like checking pending Tattler messages, empty result renderer, provider-safe text, terminate:true, and set a receive-after-agent-end flag. agent_end should defer until idle and trigger a synthetic receive turn; before_agent_start then drains the pending inbox into a persistent custom batch message. This is latency/semantics polish; correctness also works when user aborts and sends any next prompt because before_agent_start drains for every turn.
